/// A jewellery GRADING affix: which ability it grants bonus ranks to.
///
/// The magnitude is absent here, and the reason previously given for that was
/// WRONG. It said the shipped data carries none because
/// `AbilityBonusRanksStaticData` has a single field, `_abilityUid`. That is
/// true of the subclass; it extends `StandardItemPropertyStaticData`, which
/// declares `float[] _xValueByTier`, and `x_grade_properties.py` has been
/// extracting it all along — all 49 ship `[0.0, 1.0, 2.0]` with
/// `PropertyType == 3` (the un-multiplied branch of `GetRawXValue`).
///
/// That reads as tier 1 -> +1 rank and tier 2 -> +2, against the +4/+5 the
/// engine currently grants, and one measurement disagrees (a menu reading of
/// "Frostbite 4+10" on two tier-2 items). Unresolved on purpose — see
/// `grade_bonus_ranks` in the arena server. Do not wire a magnitude in here
/// until that is settled.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]
pub struct GradeProperty {
    /// The affix UUID, as it appears in `item.properties.GRADING[].id`.
    pub uuid: &'static str,
    /// Editor name, e.g. `FrostbiteBonusRanks`.
    pub editor_name: &'static str,
    /// UUID of the ability whose rank this raises.
    pub ability_uuid: &'static str,
    /// Which jewellery list it came from — Ring (two slots) or Necklace (one).
    pub slot: &'static str,
}

